# The minimal reader: the title, the source and the date, the text (headings, paragraphs, lists, a quote, an image
# placeholder, preformatted text, a rule); scrolling by keys and by a drag; Left / Right the previous / next article;
# opening marks it read; the options (Text size with arrows and OK / Cancel, Article info) by a 3 s hold on the text and by
# Ctrl+O. Accents (Korben) and Japanese (NHK) through the font fallbacks.
seed pin us-ars-technica
seed pin fr-korben
seed pin jp-nhk
seed refresh
seed refresh_on_open off
wait 900
key enter
wait 400
key enter
wait 800
key down
key enter
wait 600
expect state page reader
expect state reader_idx 1
expect text "New Linux kernel fixes the long-standing scheduler stall on small boards"
shot 01-reader
check reader
key down
key down
key down
wait 200
shot 02-scrolled
key pgdn
wait 200
shot 03-page-down
drag 0.5 0.8 0.5 0.35
wait 300
shot 04-dragged
key end
wait 300
shot 05-end
key right
wait 400
expect state reader_idx 2
shot 06-next
key left
wait 400
expect state reader_idx 1
key home
holdat 0.5 0.6 3400
wait 400
expect state popup menu
expect text "Text size"
shot 07-options
check reader-options
tap "Text size"
wait 400
expect state popup choice
expect state popup_value Medium
shot 08-text-size
check text-size
tap "<right>"
wait 200
expect state popup_value Large
tap "OK"
wait 500
expect state text_size large
shot 09-large
key ctrl-o
wait 400
tap "Text size"
wait 400
key left
key left
key enter
wait 500
expect state text_size small
shot 10-small
key ctrl-o
wait 400
tap "Article info"
wait 400
shot 11-info
key esc
wait 300
key ctrl-o
wait 400
tap "Text size"
wait 400
key right
key enter
wait 400
expect state text_size medium
key esc
wait 400
expect state page articles
shot 12-list-after-reading
key esc
wait 300
key down
key enter
wait 600
key enter
wait 600
expect state page reader
shot 13-korben-accents
key esc
wait 300
key esc
wait 300
key down
key enter
wait 600
key enter
wait 600
shot 14-nhk-japanese
